{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01262 - MONDO_18435",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Decitabine and Acute Myeloid Leukemia With Inv3(p21;q26.2) or T(3;3)(p21;q26.2) through the intermediary of Glasdegib. Decitabine is associated with multiple subtypes of acute myeloid leukemia, including Therapy-Related Acute Myeloid Leukemia and Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia, all of which are linked to Glasdegib. Glasdegib is known to be an inhibitor of the enzyme IDH1, which is frequently mutated in acute myeloid leukemia. This suggests that Decitabine may exert its effects through a mechanism involving IDH1 inhibition, potentially leading to the development of a specific subtype of acute myeloid leukemia. The overlapping pathways and indications across different subtypes of acute myeloid leukemia imply a broader role for Decitabine in the treatment of this disease. The evidence is consistent but not definitive, and further research is needed to establish a direct causal relationship.",
